Title: Conditional sum of an arithmetic progression with obfuscated init
Main goal: For each input pair (N, L), build an array flavors[i] = L + i for i = 0..N-1, and compute a sum according to these rules: 
- if L < 0 and L + N - 1 <= 0, sum flavors[0..N-2];
- else if L >= 0 and L + N - 1 > 0 (i.e., first term nonnegative and last term positive), sum flavors[1..N-1];
- else if L < 0 and L + N - 1 > 0, sum all flavors except any zero term (i = -L, if present).
Print the resulting sum for each test case. The static block initializes the array l to [0, 1] via obfuscated bitwise calculations.
